    "obsolete_caption_explanations": [
      "Table S10. The three ordinations and their comparison metrics on the published pre-QC sample set and on the analysis set. Analysis-set values from results/dimred_comparison_qcset.csv. The table is numbered after Table S12 rather than in document order so that the existing table numbers, which other sections cite, do not shift.",
      "Table S13. The six threshold scenarios, from results/sensitivity_summary.csv. Maximum pairwise FST is the Coastal savanna against Guinea savanna pair in all six. Mantel values are the censored region-level test; the uncensored p-values in the same file are 0.0413, 0.1214, 0.2002, 0.1792, 0.0644 and 0.0502. One verdict does turn on the censoring: the MAF ≥ 0.02 scenario is significant censored (0.0467) and not significant uncensored (0.0502), so on the uncensored statistic the baseline is the only scenario clearing 0.05. The other five verdicts are unchanged. The table is numbered after Table S10 so that the existing table numbers do not shift.",
      "Table S24. The three ordinations recomputed on the 1,900-isolate analysis set, beside the published 4,905-isolate run (results/dimred_comparison.csv, corrected/dimred_comparison_qcset.csv). Both columns read the same published Pf8 distance matrix; the right-hand column re-slices it to the analysis samples. Settings are identical (trustworthiness at k = 30; silhouette against zone labels). This table is new in this revision and is lettered so that the existing table numbering is unchanged.",
      "Table S28. Threshold sensitivity of the region-level Mantel test and of maximum pairwise FST (results/sensitivity_summary.csv, scripts/step13_sensitivity.py). Only the named threshold differs from the baseline in each row. \"p (as run)\" floors negative pairwise FST to zero, as step06_mantel.py does; \"p (uncensored)\" retains them, following Table S26. Negative pairs floored, in row order: 3, 4, 3, 0, 4, 4. All tests are one-sided over 9,999 permutations at seed 42. This table is new in this revision and is lettered so that the existing table numbering is unchanged."
    ]
